      "body": "`main` is `074dac167c26c1e091198f691ed5727817dba88a`. This tag now points at that commit. The previous tag object pointed at `d27530af`.\n\nLinux archives built from this tree:\n\n- `btx-0.34.16-x86_64-linux-gnu.tar.gz` SHA256 `9bbfff065299b3d6e863ecdeb0e54917788c1c0395cfa1d2b61bc40bf364932b`\n- `btx-0.34.16-x86_64-linux-gnu-cuda13.tar.gz` SHA256 `a29202a919039c50547c90a19bb48ddc9e434c9365793131d7bda3155b3822dd` (CUDA 13.3, sm_120, static cudart, `libcublasLt.so.13` beside `btxd`)\n\n`SHA256SUMS` is published with these files. It is not signed. This build host has no release signing key.\n\nThese files replace the archives whose SHA256 values were `807d033d224979f086203e0ccfdcee2a0a97d8f381c8e9144a481c5347014087` and `18c860c02e3a3f79851dc7caabcdc5dfc756fd062b4d077180c45776dc0472a7`. Those copies left libevent, libsqlite3, libzmq, and libgomp as host packages, so `btxd -version` failed on a base image. The archives now on this release contain those libraries and the libraries those packages need. libc, libstdc++, and the NVIDIA driver stay on the host.\n\nBoth archives leave out `btx-qt` and `btx-atlas`, which on this build need a glibc newer than the archive ceiling of 2.38. CPython's `termios` extension is left out for the same reason. SwapNet does not import it. Every bundled library is within GLIBC 2.38.\n\n`btxd -version` reports v0.34.16. The CUDA archive's `btx-matmul-backend-info --backend cuda` reported the CUDA backend compiled and ready on an RTX 5060 Ti (compute 12.0, runtime 13.3). The NVIDIA driver is still required and is not bundled. macOS and Windows binaries are not in this upload.\n\nModelNet and SwapNet are in this tree for broader testing. `automatic_spend_atoms` remains `\"0\"`. Further pull requests for fixes are welcome.\n"
    },
